  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =\u2016x-y\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-k)^{2}+(-k-(-1))^{2}+(2k-0)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-6k+{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}-2k+1+4{k}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14} & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14})}^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+14 & =12 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+2 & =0 \\\\ 3{k}^{2}-4k+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(3)(1)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{4}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=1$ and $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$",
